---
import './misses.css';
import { burstTrace } from './model.mjs';
const initial = burstTrace()[0];
---
<figure class="miss-figure" data-miss-burst>
 <div class="figure-heading"><span class="figure-number">Figure 1</span>Four callers after one expiry</div>
 <div class="scene">
  <div class="controls"><label>Fill ownership <select data-mode><option value="separate">Each caller loads</option><option value="shared">Share one loader</option></select></label><label>Source read <select data-duration><option value="100">100 ms</option><option value="40">40 ms</option></select></label></div>
  <div class="label" data-clock data-live>Clock 0 ms · P7 absent</div>
  <div class="counters" data-live><div><strong data-started>0</strong><span>Source reads started</span></div><div><strong data-active>0</strong><span>Source reads running</span></div><div><strong data-waiting>0</strong><span>Callers waiting</span></div><div><strong data-answered>0</strong><span>Callers answered</span></div></div>
  <div class="convergence" data-convergence aria-hidden="true"></div>
  <div class="controls"><button type="button" data-play>Play</button><button type="button" data-back>Back</button><button type="button" data-next>Next</button><button type="button" data-reset>Reset</button><div data-hold aria-hidden="true"><span></span></div><span data-step>1 / 9</span></div>
  <p class="explanation" data-explanation data-live aria-live="polite">{initial.explanation}</p>
  <details class="caller-details"><summary>Caller and loader details</summary>
  <div class="lanes"><div class="lane"><div class="label">Callers in App A</div><div data-callers data-live>{initial.callers.map(c => <div class="token"><strong>Caller {c.id} · arrives {c.at} ms</strong><span>{c.state}</span></div>)}</div></div><div class="lane"><div class="label">Source work</div><div data-loaders data-live><div class="token">No reads started</div></div></div></div>
  </details>
 </div>
 <figcaption>An invented trace. P7 means <code>product:v1:north:P7:en-GB:GBP</code>. All reads return the unchanged GBP 20.00 card. Cache lookup and fill time are omitted. At equal times, a completion happens before an arrival. Changing an option returns to the first step.</figcaption>
 <details><summary>The outcomes, as text</summary><p>At 100 ms per read, independent callers start four reads at 0, 20, 40 and 60 ms. They finish at 100, 120, 140 and 160 ms. Sharing starts one read at 0 ms and answers all four callers at 100 ms. At 40 ms per read, independent callers start two reads; sharing starts one. In both 40 ms runs, callers C and D find cache hits. The drawing counts work, not production capacity.</p></details>
</figure>
<script>
 import { stepper } from '../../figures/stepper.mjs';
 import { burstTrace } from './model.mjs';
 document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-miss-burst]').forEach(root => {
  const mode = root.querySelector<HTMLSelectElement>('[data-mode]')!;
  const duration = root.querySelector<HTMLSelectElement>('[data-duration]')!;
  let trace = burstTrace();
  const text = (selector: string, value: string | number) => { root.querySelector(selector)!.textContent = String(value); };
  const player = stepper(root, { steps: () => trace.length, draw: (step: number) => {
   const state = trace[step];
   text('[data-clock]', `Clock ${state.time} ms · P7 ${state.cached ? 'cached' : 'absent'}`);
   for (const name of ['started','active','waiting','answered']) text(`[data-${name}]`, state[name]);
   const ys = [42, 94, 146, 198];
   const shared = mode.value === 'shared';
   const routes = state.callers.filter(c => c.loader).map(c => {
    const i = state.callers.indexOf(c);
    const l = state.loaders.find(l => l.id === c.loader)!;
    const ly = shared ? 120 : ys[state.loaders.indexOf(l)];
    const path = `M 61 ${ys[i]} C 132 ${ys[i]}, 174 ${ly}, 242 ${ly}`;
    const isNew = c.at === state.time && c.state === 'Waiting';
    return `<path d="${path}" fill="none" stroke="var(--color-accent)" stroke-width="2" ${l.done ? 'stroke-dasharray="4 4"' : ''}/>${isNew ? `<circle class="travelling-request" r="5" fill="var(--color-accent)"><animateMotion dur="0.65s" repeatCount="1" path="${path}" fill="freeze"/></circle>` : ''}`;
   }).join('');
   const callerNodes = state.callers.map((c,i) => `<circle cx="42" cy="${ys[i]}" r="18" fill="var(--color-surface)" stroke="var(--color-rule-strong)" stroke-width="2"/><text x="42" y="${ys[i] + 5}" text-anchor="middle">${c.id}</text>`).join('');
   const loaderNodes = state.loaders.map((l,i) => { const y = shared ? 120 : ys[i]; return `<rect x="242" y="${y-18}" width="60" height="36" rx="4" fill="var(--color-surface)" stroke="var(--color-accent)" stroke-width="${l.done ? 1 : 3}"/><text x="272" y="${y+5}" text-anchor="middle">${l.id}${l.done ? ' ✓' : ''}</text>`; }).join('');
   root.querySelector('[data-convergence]')!.innerHTML = `<svg viewBox="0 0 330 230" role="presentation"><text x="42" y="13" text-anchor="middle">Callers</text><text x="272" y="13" text-anchor="middle">Loaders</text>${routes}${callerNodes}${loaderNodes}</svg>`;
   root.querySelector('[data-callers]')!.innerHTML = state.callers.map(c => `<div class="token" data-state="${c.state}"><strong>Caller ${c.id} · arrives ${c.at} ms</strong><span>${c.state}${c.state === 'Waiting' ? ` for ${c.loader}` : ''}</span></div>`).join('');
   root.querySelector('[data-loaders]')!.innerHTML = state.loaders.length ? state.loaders.map(l => `<div class="token" data-state="${l.done ? 'Answered' : 'Running'}"><strong>${l.id} · ${l.start}–${l.end} ms</strong><span>${l.done ? 'Finished' : 'Running'}</span></div>`).join('') : '<div class="token">No reads started</div>';
   text('[data-explanation]', state.explanation);
  }});
  for (const select of [mode, duration]) select.addEventListener('change', () => {
   trace = burstTrace({ shared: mode.value === 'shared', duration: Number(duration.value) });
   root.querySelector<HTMLButtonElement>('[data-reset]')!.click();
   player.render();
  });
 });
</script>
